What is Git?

Git is a version control system.

In simple words:
👉 It keeps track of who changed what, when, and why in your code or files.

Think of Git like “Save + History + Undo + Collaboration” for projects.

🔹 Why do we use Git?

✔ Track changes in code
✔ Go back to old versions
✔ Work with multiple people
✔ Create branches to experiment safely
✔ Avoid losing work


Check status
git status


Shows modified, staged, untracked files.

2️⃣ Initialize a repo
git init

3️⃣ Add files
git add file.txt
